Register the Orca CLI from the web client

Every agent-skill setup card (Orchestration, Browser Use, Computer Use, Linear,
Ephemeral VMs, Mobile Emulator, Settings > CLI) warned "Orca CLI registration is
unavailable" and could never register `orca-ide`, because `createCliApi()` in
the web preload was a hardcoded `supported:false` stub. The terminal those
cards open runs on the connected server, where the CLI genuinely exists.

Three runtime RPC methods - `cli.getInstallStatus`, `cli.install` and
`cli.remove` - reuse the exact `CliInstaller` behind the desktop IPC handlers,
with the same shell-path hydration so `pathConfigured` matches what a PTY sees.
All three mutate the host, so none of them is on `MOBILE_RPC_METHOD_ALLOWLIST`:
a paired phone must never register or remove host commands.

To test, open Settings > CLI in the tile, register the CLI, then run `orca-ide`
in a terminal on the workspace. Covered by `cli.test.ts` and
`mobile-rpc-allowlist.test.ts`.

